{title: 174 - Star of Our Hope}
{artist: Seventh-day Adventist Hymnal}
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: A}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{tag: Jesus Christ}
{tag: }

Verse 1:
[A/E]Star of [E]our [A]hope! He'll soon [F#m/C#]appear,
[G#dim]The [A]last [Bm]loud trumpet [G#dim]speaks [E/B]Him [D/A]near;
[A]Hail [D/A]Him, [A/C#]all [D]saints, from pole [E7/B]to [A]pole-
[G#dim]How welcome [Bm/F#]to [E/B]the [F#m/C#]faithful [E/B]soul!

Verse 2:
[A/E]From heaven [F#m]angelic [E7/D]voices [E/B]sound:
[G#dim]Behold [Bm]the Lord [A/E]of [G#dim]glory [D/A]crowned,
[A]Arrayed [D/A]in majesty [E7/B]divine,
[G#dim]And in [A/E]His [Bm/F#]highest [F#m/C#]glories [E/B]shine.

Verse 3:
[A/E]The grave [E]yields [A]up its precious [E/B]trust,
[G#dim]Which [A]long [Bm]has slumbered [G#dim]in [E/B]the [D/A]dust,
[A]Resplendent [D]forms ascending, [G#dim]fair,
[G#dim]Now meet [A/E]the [Bm/F#]Savior [F#m/C#]in the [E/B]air.

Verse 4:
[A/E]Descending with His azure [E/B]throne,
[G#dim]He [A]claims [Bm]the kingdom [G#dim]for [E/B]His [D/A]own;
[A]The [D/A]saints [A/C#]rejoice, [D]they [E7/B]shout, [A]they [G#dim]sing,
[G#dim]And hail [A/E]Him their [E/B]triumphant King.
